---
import { digitalIdentities } from '../identifiers.ts';
import LayoutGlobal from '../layouts/LayoutGlobal.astro';
import { profile, siteData } from '../utilities/microdata.ts';
import { asCanonicalUrl } from '../utilities/urls.ts';

const linkedIn = digitalIdentities.find(
	(d) => d.type === 'social' && d.name.toLowerCase() === 'linkedin',
)!;
const bluesky = digitalIdentities.find(
	(d) => d.type === 'social' && d.name.toLowerCase() === 'bluesky',
)!;
---

<LayoutGlobal
	meta={{
		title: "Adam Coster's Digital Archive",
		canonical: '/',
		description: 'Articles, identifiers, tools, and more from Adam Coster.',
		ldjsons: [siteData, profile],
		social: { image: asCanonicalUrl('/profile.portrait.1372.jpg') },
	}}
>
	<h1>About Me</h1>

	<p>
		I'm the CTO at <a href="https://www.bscotch.net">Butterscotch Shenanigans</a
		> (a.k.a. "Bscotch"). I co-founded Bscotch with my two brothers back in 2012,
		went full-time in 2014 after getting my Ph.D. (in Cellular & Molecular Biology,
		of all things), and that's been my main thing ever since.
	</p>
	<p>
		At Bscotch I've had a lot of responsibilities over the years. We're a very
		small team and have done everything we could to stay independent, which
		mostly means we've all had to wear a lot of hats. My brothers can I share
		responsibility for the business side of things, and then fall into
		specialized technical domains. Mine has been what I like to call
		"Productivity Engineering": designing and building software to make everyone
		else's work more enjoyable, reliable, and efficient. In practice that's
		largely meant full-stack web development.
	</p>
	<p>
		Check out <a href="/articles">my writings</a> and <a href="/portfolio"
			>my portfolio</a
		> to learn more.
	</p>

	<section>
		<header>
			<h2 id="identities">Finding me on the Internet</h2>
		</header>
		<p>
			The web is a hellscape of fraud, scams, and impersonation. I've assembled
			most of my digital identifiers and properties below: you can find my
			official accounts/profiles/identifiers in these places. And if someone is
			claiming to be somewhere, you should be able to verify that against the
			things listed below.
		</p>
		<p>
			(Of course someone having one of these identifiers isn't <i>proof</i>
			that it's me. You know, hackers and whatnot. But it's a infinitely more likely
			than something not listed here!)
		</p>
		<p>
			Note that I don't regularly use most of these: if you're looking to
			connect your best bet is
			<a href={bluesky.url}>Bluesky</a> or <a href={linkedIn.url}>LinkedIn</a> (infrequently
			checked).
		</p>
		<p>
			If you're looking to contact me about <a href="https://www.bscotch.net"
				>Bscotch</a
			> or <a href="https://ludokit.com">LudoKit</a> stuff, use the contact systems
			on those sites.
		</p>
		<ul>
			{
				digitalIdentities.map((identity) => (
					<li>
						<a href={identity.url}>
							{identity.name}
							{'handle' in identity && `(as ${identity.handle})`}
						</a>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</section>
</LayoutGlobal>
